+
+## Wild Zone 2: distinguish the two Great Balls
+
+The eastern pickup consistently fits archived marker 8258 better than the separate western pickup. Distances below are to the archived display point, not measured errors from physical gameplay positions. Both candidates stayed out of the fit.
+
+| Fit | East | West |
+| --- | ---: | ---: |
+| All original fit rows | 4.741 px | 121.099 px |
+| Omit Wild Zone 3 | 4.205 px | 120.759 px |
+| Omit Wild Zone 4 | 4.532 px | 120.827 px |
+| Omit Wild Zone 9 | 8.003 px | 123.272 px |
+| Omit Wild Zone 17 | 40.185 px | 146.099 px |
+
+[Gamer Guides](https://www.gamerguides.com/pokemon-legends-z-a/database/items/poke-balls/great-ball) lists two source positions. [Pokébip’s field guide](https://www.pokebip.com/page/jeux-video/legendes-pokemon-z-a/guide-des-lieux/zone-sauvage-2) describes two routes: the east pickup beyond the southeast Rock Smash obstacle and the west pickup below a large southwest rock. Prefer the east match for archive research only. Keep the west as its own discovery lead; do not reuse the existing collection key.
+
+The [original Zone 2 close-up](../../assets/atlas/wild-zones/wild-zone-02-closeup.png) shows three usable fixed bridge spans around the central island but no labelled pickup. Use their endpoints and the shoreline bends as alignment landmarks, not the session cursor or the zone badge. TM027 Swift, described by Pokébip between trees on the central island and [pictured in the GameSpot guide listing](https://www.gamespot.com/gallery/pokemon-legends-za-tm-technical-machine-locations/2900-7146/), is the next visual proof candidate. The [08:48 gameplay chapter](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t-n2eBPRqbA&t=528s) and original still were not jointly registered. No exact pickup XY, floor approval, production transform, collection change or public pin.
